{"type": "assistant", "message": {"id": "msg_1786351109016", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "tool_use", "id": "chatcmpl-tool-b732423e7800762a", "name": "Bash", "input": {"command": "PAPERS_DIR=./papers uv run paper-wiki search --paper \"2604.15804\" 2>&1 | head -60", "description": "Search paper-wiki for paper 2604.15804"}}], "model": "GLM-5.2-w4a8", "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 0, "output_tokens": 0, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0}, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "80e239b2-8a28-4502-9952-dd42607093ae", "uuid": "56b9b064-8e65-4300-9b9c-8f867372f928"}
{"type": "assistant", "message": {"id": "msg_1786351109016", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "tool_use", "id": "chatcmpl-tool-bcd1ba491010826f", "name": "Bash", "input": {"command": "PAPERS_DIR=./papers uv run paper-wiki search --concept \"Qwen3 Omni audio visual\" 2>&1 | head -40", "description": "Search paper-wiki for Qwen3 Omni"}}], "model": "GLM-5.2-w4a8", "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 0, "output_tokens": 0, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0}, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "80e239b2-8a28-4502-9952-dd42607093ae", "uuid": "856ee8ab-2107-4304-b230-cd2e5e83bc6f"}
{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-b732423e7800762a", "type": "tool_result", "content": "# Qwen3.5-Omni Technical Report\narXiv: 2604.15804\nAuthors: Qwen Team\nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: audio_understanding\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. Qwen3.5-Omni introduces a Hybrid Attention Mixture-of-Experts (MoE) architecture for both the Thinker and Talker modules to enable highly efficient long-sequence inference.\n  2. The model supports long-context modeling up to 256k tokens, accommodating over 10 hours of audio and 400 seconds of 720P video.\n  3. A multi-codebook codec representation is adopted for the Talker to enable single-frame, immediate speech synthesis.\n  4. The ARIA technique is proposed to dynamically align text and speech units during streaming decoding, significantly improving the stability and prosody of generated speech.\n  5. Multilingual training is substantially expanded to cover 113 languages and dialects for speech recognition and 36 for speech synthesis.\n  6. The model achieves controllable audio-visual captioning capable of generating screenplay-level fine-grained descriptions with precise temporal synchronization.\n  7. Comprehensive real-time interaction is enabled through semantic interruption, end-to-end voice control, and zero-shot voice customization from user samples.\n  8. Qwen3.5-Omni exhibits native omnimodal agentic behavior, including autonomous tool use and the emergent Audio-Visual Vibe Coding capability.\n  9. The model achieves state-of-the-art results across 215 audio and audio-visual benchmarks, surpassing Gemini-3.1 Pro in key audio tasks.\n\nTags: LALM, LALM/对话型, 压缩, LALM/音频标记-融合", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "80e239b2-8a28-4502-9952-dd42607093ae", "uuid": "cd46044c-fb0a-4872-9029-9d6d6fc6af2a", "timestamp": "2026-08-10T08:38:36.560Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "# Qwen3.5-Omni Technical Report\narXiv: 2604.15804\nAuthors: Qwen Team\nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: audio_understanding\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. Qwen3.5-Omni introduces a Hybrid Attention Mixture-of-Experts (MoE) architecture for both the Thinker and Talker modules to enable highly efficient long-sequence inference.\n  2. The model supports long-context modeling up to 256k tokens, accommodating over 10 hours of audio and 400 seconds of 720P video.\n  3. A multi-codebook codec representation is adopted for the Talker to enable single-frame, immediate speech synthesis.\n  4. The ARIA technique is proposed to dynamically align text and speech units during streaming decoding, significantly improving the stability and prosody of generated speech.\n  5. Multilingual training is substantially expanded to cover 113 languages and dialects for speech recognition and 36 for speech synthesis.\n  6. The model achieves controllable audio-visual captioning capable of generating screenplay-level fine-grained descriptions with precise temporal synchronization.\n  7. Comprehensive real-time interaction is enabled through semantic interruption, end-to-end voice control, and zero-shot voice customization from user samples.\n  8. Qwen3.5-Omni exhibits native omnimodal agentic behavior, including autonomous tool use and the emergent Audio-Visual Vibe Coding capability.\n  9. The model achieves state-of-the-art results across 215 audio and audio-visual benchmarks, surpassing Gemini-3.1 Pro in key audio tasks.\n\nTags: LALM, LALM/对话型, 压缩, LALM/音频标记-融合", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
